      "body_html": "I totally thought there was a thread on the cupreas, but I can't find it, so here's a new thread!  Here's a \"new\" clone that was just recently discovered....a few minutes ago!  Had no idea it was a cuprea until now!<br/><br/>S. alata var. cuprea Eastern Louisiana, pics taken 11/30/22:<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52534550926_b72f8508f7_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52534551086_56bbce259b_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>an absolute beauty! <br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52534080427_43e45f5e1b_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52535025735_24f0631686_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>the color is coppery orange, just love this one!<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52534550371_6c4aeabeb7_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>HEre's the original cuprea clone that was selected out a year or two ago, from the same location.  It's pretty darn sweet too!<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/51833099598_0792e5a182_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/51833722845_4ff957e65c_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/51832989326_bc73202543_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/51833722870_0c01eaa630_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
