      "timestamp_raw": "Dec 5, 2024 17:10:57 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "Not looking as cuprea-ey this year (they were recently divided last winter, color forms prefer to be left undisturbed to reach their fullest color potential), but nevertheless, it's a copper topped alata!  These rare and elusive clones are quite vigorous but still very uncommon in cultivation.  Photos taken 11/5/24:<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/54186110450_4d23feb02a_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/54185941838_87beba58f8_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/54185670666_7921665eec_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/54185670691_2ff9e6b6b9_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
